{"id":"F501","verdict":"accept","strength":"weak","label":"1B","direction":"supports","note":"The prices check out: 25B lane $3,380 / $3,180 (8+), kit-provided fees $4,860 (8 lanes) and $1,420 (2 lanes). The subtraction is correct. The main point, that core lane rates sit well above list, is already known (D019 has Carver at +64% per lane). What is new is only the split into a labor fee of about $608/lane and a reagent-plus-margin remainder of about 1.25–1.35x list. This is a research-core price; it does not show the vendor's net price."},
{"id":"F505","verdict":"accept","strength":"medium","label":"2B","direction":"supports","note":"The $2,599 and $2,549 25B promos are already known. The new parts are the 2023–24 launch price of $2,799 (with a ≥16-lane condition) and the 10B series. The claim's '−12%' does not match the detail's −13.5% / −16.6%; the like-for-like single-lane move is about −13.5% over about 30 months, or about −5.6%/yr (see derived item). This supports continued price erosion, but at a rate well below the thesis's 'accelerating' view."},
{"id":"F508","verdict":"accept","strength":"medium","label":"2A","direction":"supports","note":"The deduplication logic is confirmed for 6D06353301: row 00425 has original C$630,439.40 + amendment C$14,410.12 = contract value C$644,849.52, i.e. cumulative. But the API comments show amendment rows are not reliably cumulative (C-2024-2025-Q4-00116 has original C$1.00M and contract value C$0.40M). FY24-25 may therefore hold similar distortions. Downgraded from strong. PHAC is a public-health and microbiology buyer, not academic research, so it is a weak proxy for 2A."},
{"id":"F509","verdict":"accept","strength":"strong","label":"2A","direction":"supports","note":"Verified: row C-2025-2026-Q4-00425 (2026-02-04, PHAC, type A) has contract value C$644,849.52 = C$630,439.40 + C$14,410.12, so counting both rows double-counts. The corrected −53% PHAC H1 figure follows. The all-federal −22% depends on the earlier total having included both rows, which is plausible but unconfirmed."},
